 "traditions": [],
 "notes": "All four planned kinds kept (old k106–k109; 'X effect' renamed 'X pedal'); kind s now Wikipedia 'Distortion (music)', which defines all four. Archetypes: 7 overdrive, 4 distortion, 5 fuzz, 3 boost. Old models folded into archetype versions (JHS 3 Series Screamer, Lil' RAT, RAT, DS-1, DS-2, MT-2, Distortion+, PackRat, Magus Pro, Metal Muff, DOD 250); UA 'Enigmatic '82 Overdrive Special Amp' merged with 'UAFX Enigmatic '82'. Dropped retailer ranges 'Effects' (NUX), 'Stompboxes' (Boss), 'TS Series' (covered by the archetype), 'Big Muff'/'Rat' ranges (now archetypes). Left out for lack of a retrieved page: Univox Super-Fuzz, Rush Pepbox (maker unclear), King of Tone, Keeley/Strymon/Wampler/EarthQuaker register entries (founding facts unsure), years for BD-2W, Micro Amp launch year (zzounds 403; electrosmash DNS failure), Boss HM-2 year. Marshall uses register name 'Marshall' (old data 'Marshall Amplification'); Dunlop and JHS Pedals brand entries from knowledge."
